## Architecture and Refactoring

A large part of the course involved improving code that already worked.

Refactoring included:

- Replacing unused or outdated classes and constructors.
- Replacing parallel inventory arrays with structured `ItemEntry` objects.
- Consolidating repeated combat and status-processing logic.
- Moving investigation behavior into `EncounterManager`.
- Moving room configuration into shared room definitions.
- Improving room lookup using pointers and references.
- Separating presentation logic from gameplay state.
- Creating shared console-formatting helpers.
- Improving ownership boundaries between managers and game objects.
- Reducing unnecessary temporary objects and duplicated logic.
- Improving C++17 portability between compilers.

These changes made it easier to understand which classes owned data and which systems only referenced it.

